  "id": "c9bdec4f-0c76-5042-8d92-b072f210728a",
  "slug": "air-fryer-chicken-parmesan-recipe-8698442",
  "name": "Air Fryer Chicken Parmesan",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "The air fryer is perfect for making chicken Parmesan. No need to fuss with deep-frying and the chicken turns out cruspy and golden brown with lots of cheese and sauce.",
  "cuisine": "Italian",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Gather all ingredients."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "On a cutting board, butterfly chicken by cutting each breast in half widthwise to create 4 thin pieces of chicken; season both sides with 1/2 teaspoon of the salt and 1/4 teaspoon of the black pepper."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Place flour, egg, and panko in 3 separate shallow dishes. Add Parmesan, oil, crushed red pepper, and garlic powder to panko; stir to coat. Add remaining 1/4 teaspoon salt and remaining 1/4 teaspoon black pepper to flour; stir to combine. Working with 1 chicken piece at a time, dredge chicken in flour; shake off excess. Dip in egg; let excess drip off. Dredge in panko mixture to coat; place on a plate."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Preheat a 6-quart air fryer to 400 degrees F (200 degrees C) for 2 minutes. Working in two batches, add 2 chicken cutlets to the air fryer basket in a single layer. Cook until chicken is golden brown on both sides, about 5 minutes per side."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Top each chicken piece with 1/4 cup marinara and 1/4 cup mozzarella cheese."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Snugly fit all 4 breasts in a single layer in air fryer basket; cook at 400 degrees F (200 degrees C) until cheese is melted and browned and a thermometer inserted into the thickest portion of chicken registers 165 degrees F (73 degrees C), 2 to 3 minutes. Recipe developed by Amanda Stanfield"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 4,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 25,
